{"call_id":"d3218ada0721fdc8","request_hash":"d4a63f5f3127d74454e3427b045e26dcdbf52de2d16b5cdf148bdd48918d0786","model_label":"gpt-6.1-sol","mode":"answer","cell":{"item":"SHARED-000","condition":"p2-large"},"source":"cache","attempts":0,"result":{"request_hash":"d4a63f5f3127d74454e3427b045e26dcdbf52de2d16b5cdf148bdd48918d0786","provider":"openai","model_requested":"gpt-6.1-sol","model_returned":"gpt-6.1-sol","text":"If your Halvard Home Keel washing machine vibrates more than usual:\n\n1. **Pause the programme and wait for the drum to stop** before checking it. [P1]\n2. If the door unlocks, spread heavy items, such as towels, evenly around the drum, then restart the programme. **Do not force the door open.** [P1]\n3. Check that the machine stands firmly on a hard, level floor, with all four feet touching the floor and no rocking when gently pushed at opposite corners. [P1] Switch it off and unplug it before adjusting its feet. [P4]\n4. If it was newly installed, check the installation guide to confirm that the transit bolts were removed. [P1]\n5. If strong vibration continues, **stop using the machine and contact Halvard Home support**. [P1]\n\nIf the shaking is severe, stop using the appliance, switch it off and disconnect it from the electricity supply if safe to do so. [P2]","input_tokens":2257,"output_tokens":211,"reasoning_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0,"time_to_first_answer_token_ms":1134.0001001954079,"time_to_first_thinking_ms":null,"total_latency_ms":4197.374099865556,"finish_reason":"stop","timestamp_utc":"2026-10-18T22:01:10.177485+00:00","error":null},"error":null,"recorded_utc":"2026-10-18T22:10:15.771563+00:00"}
